# Derived: regenerable machine output. Opt a subtree back in with a '!' rule when a
# project wants its metadata committed as a contract (see README.md, "Track policy").
metadata/**
!metadata/**/
!metadata/**/README.md

# Belt and braces for DEC-026 section 4, and for the rule that a report records a PATH to a
# source file rather than a copy of it: a .java under .jcodebuddy/ is always a mistake, so it
# stays ignored even after a project opts metadata/entity in as a contract with the '!' rule
# above. An older tooling did drop generated source here (codebuddy.md section 6.1); this line
# is what stops that residue from ever being committed, and GeneratorGuardTest asserts the tree
# itself stays clear of it.
metadata/**/*.java

# The module index (DEC-028) is coupled to the metadata above: a document names source files by ids
# that resolve only in index/files.json, so a project that opts metadata/ in MUST opt index/ in too,
# or its committed documents reference an uncommitted table. Same shape as the metadata rules: the
# subtree is derived and ignored, and only its README.md is re-included; README.md shows the two
# opt-in snippets side by side.
index/**
!index/**/
!index/**/README.md

# Disposable: run logs, probes, temp copies. Never a deliverable.
agent-state/**
